  "question": {
    "text": "A beam of light consists of two wavelengths, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6300</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Å</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5600</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Å</mi></math>. This beam of light is used to obtain an interference pattern in YDSE. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>th</mi></msup></math> bright fringe of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6300</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Å</mi></math> coincides with the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi>th</mi></msup></math> dark fringe of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5600</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Å</mi></math> from the central line, then find the value of <em><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></math></em>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Fringe width&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Δw</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>6300</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Å</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5600</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Å</mi></math>; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Δw</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5600</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Å</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mfrac></math><br /><br />So <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>th</mi></msup></math> bright fringe position of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6300</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Å</mi></math> is at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>6300</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Å</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mfrac></math>.<br /><br />So for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi>th</mi></msup></math> dark fringe of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5600</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Å</mi></math> is at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>5600</mn><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mfrac></math>.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6300</mn><mo>×</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5600</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>63</mn></mrow><mn>56</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>",
